Spec: Native Windows control listener

Purpose:
  Admit only the current Windows user to a bounded local control session.

Owns:
  ./PipeHost.cs

Must:
  Create the first pipe instance with a protected current-user DACL and reject remote clients.
  Capture the actual impersonated client SID after reading and compare it to the host SID before dispatch.
  Bound each read/write to two seconds and keep one connection active with at most `32` requests.
  After the final response, allow up to two seconds for peer consumption before recycling the native instance.
  Retain the first pipe handle across sessions, reject occupied names and release identity tokens after checks.
  Cancel pending accepts and reads on shutdown without affecting installed services.
  Recover if a client closes before the native accept starts.
  Capture the held pipe-client process identity for registration-enabled hosts before dispatch.
  Keep pending-grant requests disabled unless explicitly selected by the host.
  Share the protected first-instance pipe factory with one-use secure data attachments and keep secure streams disabled unless explicitly supplied by the host.
